## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of end-to-end AWS data pipelines using AI services, speaker diarization, secure data handling, error management, IAM least-privilege principles, and cost optimization for beginner-level implementations.

## Key Concepts

- Event-driven architecture: S3 → Lambda → Amazon Transcribe → DynamoDB
- Transcribe diarization for per-speaker transcript segmentation
- Multi-format output storage (full + individual speaker transcripts)
- DynamoDB indexing strategy with composite keys
- IAM security with least-privilege access patterns
- Error handling with retries and dead-letter queues
- Data privacy through KMS encryption and access controls
- Cost monitoring and optimization for short audio clips

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Lambda: S3 event handling to start Transcribe
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const record = event.Records[0];
  const bucket = record.s3.bucket.name;
  const key = record.s3.object.key;

  // Start Transcribe job with diarization
  const transcribeParams = {
    TranscriptionJobName: `interview-${Date.now()}`,
    LanguageCode: 'en-US',
    MediaFormat: key.split('.').pop(),
    Media: { MediaFileUri: `s3://${bucket}/${key}` },
    Settings: {
      ShowSpeakerLabels: true,
      MaxSpeakerLabels: 10
    },
    OutputBucketName: process.env.OUTPUT_BUCKET
  };

  await transcribe.startTranscriptionJob(transcribeParams).promise();
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-account data flows with privacy and governance, real-time ML inference, and cost controls in an enterprise multi-tenant environment.

## Key Concepts
- Event-driven architecture: S3 Events → Lambda → SageMaker → DynamoDB
- Data privacy: PII masking via pattern matching, KMS encryption at rest/transit
- Data governance: Glue Data Catalog for lineage and schema registry
- Cross-account access: RAM shared resources with service control policies
- Operational excellence: Idempotent writes (deduplication via record keys), DLQ for failures, exponential backoff

## Code Example
```javascript
export const handler = async (event) => {
  const { bucket, key } = event.Records[0].s3.object;
  const data = await s3.getObject({ Bucket: bucket, Key: key }).promise();

  const masked = maskPII(data);
  const { predictions } = await sageMaker.invokeEndpoint({
    EndpointName: process.env.ENDPOINT_NAME,
    ContentType: 'application/json',
    Body: JSON.stringify(masked)
  }).promise();

  const item = { id: uuid(), timestamp: Date.now(), scores: predictions, recordKey: key };
  await dynamo.put({ TableName: process.env.TABLE_NAME, Item: item, ConditionExpression: 'attribute_not_exists(id)' }).promise();

  await glue.updateTable({ DatabaseName: 'lineage', TableInput: tableInput });
};
```

